  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "What they say",
   "texto": [
    "**-대요** es la forma coloquial contraída de citar una afirmación: 가다 → **간대요** (dicen que va), 먹다 → **먹는대요** (dicen que come), 피곤하다 → **피곤하대요** (dicen que está cansado), 학생이다 → **학생이래요** (dicen que es estudiante). Depending on the context, it equals «They say» or «I've been told that»."
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Variance with -",
   "texto": [
    "**-다고 해요** is the uncontracted affirmative quote; **-대요** is the contrasted and frequent form in the conversation. Both transmit an attributed claim to another source: do not simply distinguish as «what someone said» against «a rumor»."
   ]
  },
